# Bulletproof Automations Training — example environment
#
# Copy to .env for local development. .env is gitignored; this file is not, so
# it must never carry a real value.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Read by scripts/build.js. These two, and only these two.
#
# The build substitutes them into dist/ wherever the __SUPABASE_URL__ and
# __SUPABASE_ANON_KEY__ tokens appear. The same two names must be set on the
# Cloudflare Pages project, for BOTH Production and Preview — a build with
# CF_PAGES set and either value missing exits 1 rather than shipping a dead
# enrollment form.
#
# Supabase dashboard -> Settings -> API:
#   SUPABASE_URL       the "Project URL"
#   SUPABASE_ANON_KEY  the key labelled "anon" / "public". Newer projects label
#                      it "publishable" and issue it as sb_publishable_… rather
#                      than the older eyJ… JWT. Either is fine.
#
# Both are PUBLIC values. The anon key reaches every visitor's browser; what
# protects the data is row-level security, not the key being secret.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

SUPABASE_URL=https://YOUR_PROJECT_REF.supabase.co
SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=YOUR_SUPABASE_PUBLIC_KEY

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Supabase CLI and Management API. NOT read by this build.
#
# Optional. Needed only for running SQL, inspecting policies, and managing
# migrations from the command line instead of the dashboard.
#
# SUPABASE_PROJECT_REF   The <ref> from https://<ref>.supabase.co
# SUPABASE_ACCESS_TOKEN  Personal access token, sbp_… — Account settings ->
#                        Access Tokens. ACCOUNT-WIDE: it reaches every project
#                        you own, and can run SQL as the database owner, so it
#                        can read and rewrite the enrollment roll. Revocable in
#                        one click without affecting the anon key or the site.
# SUPABASE_DB_PASSWORD   Only for supabase link / db pull / db push. Ad-hoc SQL
#                        goes through the Management API and does not need it.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

SUPABASE_PROJECT_REF=YOUR_PROJECT_REF
SUPABASE_ACCESS_TOKEN=YOUR_SUPABASE_ACCESS_TOKEN
SUPABASE_DB_PASSWORD=YOUR_DATABASE_PASSWORD

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# PAYSTACK — read by the Cloudflare Pages Functions at runtime, not by the
# build. Set on the Pages project, for Production AND Preview separately.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# PAYSTACK_SECRET_KEY   sk_test_… or sk_live_…
#
# There is only one variable, and it is the whole mode switch. The key's own
# prefix says which environment it belongs to, so a separate PAYSTACK_MODE flag
# could only ever disagree with it:
#
#   unset       the reservation flow. The form records the enrollment and the
#               page says we will make contact — exactly how the site behaved
#               before Paystack existed. This is the safe default and it is
#               what production runs until the account is activated.
#   sk_test_…   checkout is offered ONLY to a request that opted in, which the
#               page does only when loaded as ?paystack=test. Nobody can reach
#               a test checkout by accident and believe they have paid.
#   sk_live_…   checkout for everyone. Pasting this in is the entire activation
#               step: no code change, no copy change, no redeploy needed beyond
#               the one Cloudflare does when the variable changes.
#
# NEVER expose this to the browser. It is read inside functions/api/, which
# runs on Cloudflare's edge; it is not a build-time token and must never be
# added to scripts/build.js.

PAYSTACK_SECRET_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NOT read by this build, and deliberately not listed above.
#
# The Supabase Edge Functions and the Daily Waitlist Digest action need a
# service_role key. It bypasses row-level security completely — anyone holding
# it can read and rewrite the entire enrollment roll — so it belongs in the
# Supabase dashboard under Edge Function secrets, and in GitHub Actions
# secrets, never in a file on a laptop and never in this repo.
#
# Note also that supabase/functions/ and the daily-digest workflow still point
# at the OLD Supabase project, alongside the retiring legacy routes. Anything
# configured for them is separate from the two values above, which belong to
# the current training project.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# The paystack-webhook Edge Function needs its own copies, set in the SUPABASE
# dashboard under Edge Function secrets — not here and not on Cloudflare:
#
#   PAYSTACK_SECRET_KEY        the live key, sk_live_…
#   PAYSTACK_TEST_SECRET_KEY   the test key, sk_test_… Setting this is how you
#                              switch test webhooks on; removing it switches
#                              them off, and neither affects live payments.
#   PROJECT_URL                https://<ref>.supabase.co
#   SERVICE_ROLE_KEY           bypasses RLS; required to write the roll
#
# Both keys are held there because Paystack signs test and live events with
# different keys and posts them to separately configured webhook URLs, both of
# which can point at the same function. See the header of
# supabase/functions/paystack-webhook/index.ts.
